          "lang": "en",
          "outlet_id": "france24",
          "published_at": 1790677705,
          "summary": "French firefighters went on strike on Monday to demand additional resources and staff, after the country experienced its worst wildfires in decades this summer. They're also expected to join public sector workers in Tuesday's nationwide protest, and could continue to strike until October to put pressure on the government before it approves the 2027 budget.",
          "text_hash": 15718509411963563948,
          "title": "French firefighters join nationwide protests after devastating summer wildfires"
        },
        {
          "canonical_url": "https://france24.com/en/video/20260929-french-civil-servants-strike-demand-additional-budgetary-resources",
          "cluster_id": 14774766661040220925,
          "fetched_at": 1790715376,
          "id": 11601848136729257472,
          "joined_at": 1790715376,
          "lang": "en",
          "outlet_id": "france24",
          "published_at": 1790692829,
          "summary": "French civil servants were mobilising in large numbers on Tuesday, with more than 170 rallies planned across France. A coalition of unions are demanding additional budgetary resources for schools, hospitals, and other public services. Among those on strike are firefighters, pushed to their limits by the summer's historic wildfires. Here's a look at one of the protests in Lyon.",
          "text_hash": 14031963709711587862,
          "title": "French civil servants strike, demand additional budgetary resources"
        }
      ],
      "outlet_id": "france24"
    },
